{<layer>}}}`","--write path: 'DEEP-MERGE under `data[\"mapping\"]`' via `_emit_config_toml`"],"finding":"The default (no --write) stdout serialization path is under-specified: AC1 says it emits a `[tool.rebar.mapping]` block, but the approach body describes building `{\"projects\": {<KEY>: {<layer>}}}` and the --write path serializes under the top-level key `data[\"mapping\"]` via `_emit_config_toml`. The plan does not state which top-level header the stdout output uses (`[tool.rebar.mapping]` vs `[mapping]`) nor which emitter renders stdout.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"faeb6fe828f3fb761","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Emit; AC test_probe_emits_mapping","norm_id":"n33b8796c78122506","priority":0.22,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Specify that stdout builds `{\"mapping\": {\"projects\": {<KEY>: {...}}}}` (or the `tool.rebar.mapping` variant per S1) and renders via `_emit_nested_toml(\"mapping\", ...)`, and pin the header string the AC test greps for.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Record the manual live-smoke verification as a named/tracked acceptance step (or a NAMED follow-up) so the real jira.JIRA getter boundary has an owned verification, since the offline fake never exercises it.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Tests use a FAKE probe port returning canned ... data — fully offline'","'A live smoke run is manual, never a CI gate.' — no named tracking artifact for the live-path verification"],"finding":"The offline test suite exercises the probe's per-axis getters only through a FAKE port; the real pycontribs `jira.JIRA` method boundary is never invoked in an automated test, so a wrong method name/signature on a real getter would still pass green. The plan defers live exercise to a manual smoke run but does not name it as a tracked/child acceptance step.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f95d84c2006dc6458","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing section; 'A live smoke run is manual, never a CI gate.'","norm_id":"n425dd49d0cde1f83","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A pycontribs getter name is mistyped (e.g. `issue_link_types` vs actual) — every offline test passes, but the command fails the first time a user runs it live"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Pin the exact pycontribs 3.x method names and call signatures for `issue_types`, `priorities`, `statuses`, `issue_link_types`, `createmeta_issuetypes`, `createmeta_fieldtypes` against the installed `jira` lib or its 3.x docs (record MATCH/version), since none is confirmed in-repo and only search_issues/transitions/fields are Verified.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the vocabulary getters are documented pycontribs 3.x public API' — asserted, not observed","In-repo confirmation exists ONLY for search_issues (transport) and transitions (transitions.py:80); `issue_types()`/`priorities()`/`statuses()` appear only inside S8's own mapping_probe.py port and doctor_mapping (which is itself the S-series consumer), never against a bare jira.JIRA client","resolve_symbol UNRESOLVED for jira / jira.JIRA.issue_types / .priorities / .statuses / .issue_link_types / .createmeta_issuetypes / .createmeta_fieldtypes (jira extra not installed) — Unverified, not Contradicted","Evidence class: Verified (search_issues, transitions, build_client_from_settings) + Unverified (the six getters and their exact arity/signatures across the >=3.8,<4 range)"],"finding":"Six pycontribs `jira.JIRA` methods the probe depends on — `issue_types()`, `priorities()`, `statuses()`, `issue_link_types()`, `createmeta_issuetypes(<KEY>)`, `createmeta_fieldtypes(<KEY>, <id>)` — are asserted as 'documented pycontribs 3.x public API' but are UNVERIFIED: none is exercised against a real jira.JIRA client elsewhere in the repo (only search_issues/transitions/fields are confirmed in-repo), and the jira package is not importable here to observe the surface.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3d69437599330509","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Axis grounding' bullets; pin `jira>=3.8,<4` (pyproject.toml:202)","norm_id":"nb5c33a21ea26df0c","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A pycontribs 3.x release within >=3.8,<4 renames or changes the arity of createmeta_issuetypes/createmeta_fieldtypes (createmeta APIs have churned across jira releases), causing a live-probe AttributeError/TypeError that offline fake-port tests cannot catch","issue_link_types()/statuses()/priorities() return element shapes differing from the assumed .name attribute, silently emitting empty vocabulary in the suggested block"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a short verification note to the Approach citing the pycontribs 3.8 API reference (or a one-off import against the installed jira extra) for each of the six getters, capturing the exact signature (especially createmeta_issuetypes/createmeta_fieldtypes positional args) and confirming stability across >=3.8,<4; if createmeta signatures vary within that range, narrow the pin or route a 1-hour spike to confirm before implementing.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify error handling for the live Jira probe: a per-call timeout, and how auth/permission/not-found/network errors are caught and surfaced as an actionable message (degraded/partial emission vs. clean failure) rather than an unhandled exception.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'a probe PORT with one narrow method per axis, each a thin call to a pycontribs jira.JIRA method'","No mention of timeout, retry, or error surfacing when the live Jira dependency is down/slow/returns an error"],"finding":"The live-Jira probe issues many pycontribs `jira.JIRA` calls (issue_types, priorities, issue_link_types, statuses, createmeta, search_issues, transitions) but the plan specifies no error handling for the external boundary: no timeout, no graceful degradation, and no statement of how errors (auth failure, project not found, permission denied on createmeta, network failure, slow/unavailable Jira) are surfaced to the user rather than crashing with a raw traceback.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f88227c33bbd82e38","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Axis grounding (mapping_probe.py probe port)","norm_id":"n7a58d370609430d4","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["User runs `rebar bridge suggest-mapping BADKEY` against a project they lack browse permission for → createmeta/search_issues raises; without handling the command dumps a stack trace instead of an actionable message","Jira instance is slow or unreachable → probe hangs or crashes with an opaque error and no partial/degraded output"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate the probe command's non-happy-path outcomes (invalid/nonexistent project key, empty vocabulary, missing createmeta permission) and state the user-visible result (error message + exit code, or note-annotated partial block) for each.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["T6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC covers 'discovered vocabulary ... identity-seed axis maps, and create_defaults stubs' — the happy path","Plan handles hierarchy-absent and transitions-partial but not invalid-project-key, empty-result, or permission-denied invocation outcomes"],"finding":"The command is a new user-facing CLI flow, but the plan enumerates non-happy-path behavior only for two axes (hierarchy absent → dropped+note; transitions → best-effort). It does not name the highest-stakes failure interactions for the invocation itself: an invalid/nonexistent PROJECT key, empty vocabulary results, or missing createmeta permission — nor what stdout/exit behavior the user sees in those cases.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcb38a43932a675e2","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Emit; AC test_probe_emits_mapping","norm_id":"n7f4d6d364e4b2092","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["User passes a project key that does not exist → unclear whether the command emits an empty block, errors, or writes nothing","createmeta is restricted for the user → unclear whether create_defaults is silently omitted with a note or the command fails"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the create-baseline citation: the function is `_map_local_to_jira_fields` (body at `outbound_fields.py:165-220`), not `map_local_to_remote` at `140-158` — the latter name lives in `adapters/jira/backend.py`.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.155,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"the outbound create path adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:140-158 (map_local_to_remote) already supplies summary, description, issuetype, priority, assignee, conditionally status+parent\"","search_files: `def map_local_to_remote` matches only in backend.py (:73,:219) and tests, NOT outbound_fields.py","outbound_fields.py:117 defines `_map_local_to_jira_fields`; the result dict with summary/description/issuetype/assignee is at 165-170, priority at 173-175, status at 178-180, parent at 218-220"],"finding":"The AC-footer premise cites `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:140-158 (map_local_to_remote)` as the create baseline, but no function named `map_local_to_remote` exists in `outbound_fields.py`; the actual create-baseline builder there is `_map_local_to_jira_fields`, whose baseline-field body is at lines 165-220 (line 140-158 is docstring prose). `map_local_to_remote` is a different, backend-layer function (`adapters/jira/backend.py:73`/`:219`).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f52355e56835578a5","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — 'create_defaults baseline (concrete)' footer","norm_id":"nb96b5e6c976b9bd6","priority":0.595,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer opens outbound_fields.py:140-158 expecting map_local_to_remote and finds a docstring, or edits the wrong (backend.py) function when computing the createmeta required-beyond-baseline stub set."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Replace 'adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:140-158 (map_local_to_remote)' with 'adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py `_map_local_to_jira_fields` (baseline result dict at ~165-220)'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":